{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6xepWqgb6xHq2uonMM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `parse_line` and `summarize` in `logstats/parse.py`, and all 4 tests pass. `tests/` was empty, so I wrote those tests myself in `tests/test_parse.py`. They cover a full line, a line without `bytes`, malformed inputs, the `sample.log` summary, and empty input.\n\nA few choices the format doc leaves open:\n- **Malformed lines:** a line must have 5 or 6 whitespace-separated fields. Any of these also makes it malformed: a non-uppercase method, a non-numeric status, latency or bytes, a timestamp that doesn't parse or has no timezone, or a `nan` latency.\n- **Blank lines:** `summarize` skips them without counting them as malformed.\n- **Percentiles:** p50 and p95 use nearest-rank, as the doc specifies.\n\nOn `sample.log` the summary gives 5 parsed records and 1 malformed line."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3147,"cache_read_input_tokens":24131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3147},"output_tokens":309,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1de7d7d0-77db-47ac-8ae3-ebe3b0737eb5","uuid":"c302abc5-78bc-4e24-bc0c-83ac64dcc20c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:03:19.736Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs6xeX9pJ276hjvvYWEf"}
